.TH MACHARDEN 1 "2026-09-12" "macharden 1.1.0" "macOS Security Manual"
.SH NAME
macharden \- macOS Security Hardening & Audit Scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macharden
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR | \fB\-\-category\fR \fIcategory\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR | \fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR | \fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR | \fB\-\-quiet\fR]
[\fB\-\-fix\fR]
[\fB\-\-generate\-fix\fR [\fIfile\fR]]
[\fB\-\-no\-color\fR]
[\fB\-\-compliance\fR \fIframework\fR]
[\fB\-\-daemon\-install\fR [\fIschedule\fR]]
[\fB\-\-daemon\-uninstall\fR]
[\fB\-\-daemon\-status\fR]
[\fB\-\-alert\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B macharden
is a modular, non-destructive security auditing, posture assessment, and
automated remediation tool designed exclusively for Apple macOS systems
(macOS 12 Monterey, macOS 13 Ventura, macOS 14 Sonoma, macOS 15 Sequoia,
and later).
.PP
The tool performs comprehensive security health checks against system
configuration settings, system services, networking daemons, local storage
security, exposed credentials, and persistence mechanisms. Results are
evaluated against industry-standard benchmarks such as CIS (Center for
Internet Security), NIST SP 800-53, and the MITRE ATT&CK Matrix for
Enterprise (macOS).
.PP
By default,
.B macharden
runs purely in read-only inspection mode. It computes an aggregate, weighted
.B Hardening Index
(0.0% to 100.0%) reflecting the overall defense posture of the host, details
individual findings with actionable rationales, and optionally outputs reports
to terminal, JSON, Markdown, or HTML formats.
.PP
When remediation is needed,
.B macharden
can either interactively prompt and execute fixes (\fB\-\-fix\fR) or generate
a standalone, self-contained shell script (\fB\-\-generate\-fix\fR) for review
and execution under administrative privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a summary of available command-line options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the current program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-category " " \fIcategory\fR
Execute audit checks only for the specified security category. Supported values:
.RS
.TP
.B hardening
Core operating system configuration, System Integrity Protection (SIP),
Gatekeeper, FileVault full-disk encryption, automatic software updates,
firmware password, Secure Boot, and screen lock timeouts.
.TP
.B network
Application Firewall, stealth mode (ICMP echo suppression), open listening
ports, Remote Login (SSH), Apple Remote Desktop, AirDrop, Internet Sharing,
and file sharing daemons.
.TP
.B secrets
Detection of unencrypted SSH private keys, AWS and cloud API credentials,
cleartext tokens in shell history files, exposed configuration files, and
keychain permissions.
.TP
.B persistence
Detection of unauthorized or suspicious LaunchDaemons, LaunchAgents,
privileged helper tools, user/system crontabs, and Login Items.
.TP
.B all
Execute all audit checks across every category (default behavior).
.RE
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIformat\fR
Select the output report presentation format. Supported values:
.RS
.TP
.B term
Human-readable, colorized terminal summary featuring tables, categorized status
banners, and hardening grade indicators (default).
.TP
.B json
Machine-readable, structured JSON output adhering to a validated schema,
containing detailed metadata, system telemetry, individual check statuses,
weights, and raw remediation commands. Ideal for CI/CD integration, SIEM
ingestion, and automated pipelines.
.TP
.B markdown
Comprehensive GitHub-flavored Markdown document containing executive summaries,
benchmark alignment matrices, and copy-pasteable remediation playbooks.
.TP
.B html
Standalone, single-file HTML report featuring responsive CSS styling, score
dashboard cards, filtering, and visual status badges suitable for management
review and compliance archival.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIfile\fR
Write the report output to the specified filesystem path instead of stdout.
When saving a \fBterm\fR format report to a file, ANSI escape sequences are
automatically stripped to maintain clean plaintext formatting.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Minimal output mode. Suppresses verbose per-check progress indicators and ASCII
art banners, printing only the final executive summary and score.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Interactively step through each failed check or warning that provides an
automated fix. Prompts the user before applying each command, displaying the
remediation command and rationale. Supports applying individual fixes (\fBy\fR),
skipping (\fBn\fR), applying all remaining fixes (\fBa\fR), or aborting
(\fBq\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-generate\-fix " [" \fIfile\fR ]
Generate a standalone, executable Zsh remediation script containing all
corrective commands necessary to resolve detected failures and warnings.
If \fIfile\fR is omitted, a default filename (such as \fBfix_hardening.sh\fR or
a timestamped variant) is created in the current working directory. The
generated script is marked executable (\fBchmod +x\fR) and includes pre-flight
safety checks.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color codes and text formatting in terminal output. This can also
be enabled by setting the \fBNO_COLOR\fR environment variable to any non-empty
value.
.TP
.BR \-\-compliance " " \fIframework\fR
Filter or align the audit checks with a specific security compliance framework:
.RS
.TP
.B cis
Center for Internet Security (CIS) Apple macOS Benchmark.
.TP
.B nist
National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) Special Publication
800-53 Rev. 5 and the NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF).
.TP
.B mitre
MITRE ATT&CK Matrix for Enterprise (macOS Tactical Techniques).
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon\-install " [" \fIschedule\fR ]
Install and schedule a background LaunchAgent in
\fB~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.macharden.daemon.plist\fR to run periodic
security audits. The optional \fIschedule\fR parameter can be \fBdaily\fR,
\fBweekly\fR (default), \fBmonthly\fR, \fBhourly\fR, \fBon-login\fR, or an
interval in seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon\-uninstall
Unload and remove the background LaunchAgent and associated scheduled tasks.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon\-status
Display the current status of the background monitoring daemon, including
LaunchAgent registration, PID, configured interval, and execution logs in
\fB~/.macharden/logs/\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-alert
Dispatch a native macOS desktop notification via Notification Center if
critical hardening issues or secrets leaks are identified during the audit scan.
.SH AUDIT CATEGORIES
.B macharden
organizes security checks into four primary domains:
.TP
.B 1. System Hardening (\fBhardening\fR)
Evaluates critical macOS system integrity settings. Verifies that System
Integrity Protection (SIP) is fully enabled, Gatekeeper is active with
developer validation, FileVault full-disk encryption is active, Automatic
Software Updates and security response updates are configured, screen saver
password delay is set to immediate, Remote Apple Events are disabled, and
firmware/Secure Boot integrity is maintained.
.TP
.B 2. Network Security (\fBnetwork\fR)
Evaluates local network exposure and daemon attack surfaces. Checks that the
macOS Application Firewall is enabled, stealth mode is enabled to drop
unsolicited ICMP and probe packets, unnecessary open listening ports (TCP/UDP)
are identified, SSH Remote Login is either secured or disabled, Remote Desktop
/ Apple Remote Desktop is disabled if not required, AirDrop is restricted,
and Internet Sharing is turned off.
.TP
.B 3. Secrets & Credentials (\fBsecrets\fR)
Inspects the filesystem and user environment for exposed secrets that could
lead to credential harvesting. Scans for unencrypted private SSH keys, AWS/cloud
API credentials in plain files, tokens leaked into shell history files
(\fB.zsh_history\fR, \fB.bash_history\fR), world-readable dotfiles, and
insecure file permissions on sensitive directories.
.TP
.B 4. Persistence Mechanisms (\fBpersistence\fR)
Scans locations frequently abused by malware and attackers for persistence
on macOS. Inspects LaunchDaemons (\fB/Library/LaunchDaemons\fR,
\fB/System/Library/LaunchDaemons\fR), LaunchAgents
(\fB~/Library/LaunchAgents\fR, \fB/Library/LaunchAgents\fR), scheduled cron
jobs, Login Items, privileged helper tools, and third-party
kernel/system extensions.
.SH SCORING ALGORITHM
The
.B Hardening Index
is calculated as a normalized percentage (0.0% to 100.0%) based on weighted
evaluations:
.IP \(bu 3
Each check is assigned a criticality weight (\fBW\fR) between 1 and 10 points.
.IP \(bu 3
Checks with status \fBPASS\fR earn 100% of their weight.
.IP \(bu 3
Checks with status \fBWARN\fR earn 50% of their weight.
.IP \(bu 3
Checks with status \fBFAIL\fR earn 0% of their weight.
.IP \(bu 3
Checks with status \fBINFO\fR or \fBSUGG\fR are excluded from the total point
denominator to ensure informational items do not unfairly penalize system score.
.PP
The resulting Hardening Index maps to a grade:
.RS
.TP
.B 90.0% \- 100.0%
Grade A (Hardened / Excellent Posture)
.TP
.B 80.0% \- 89.9%
Grade B (Good Posture / Minor Hardening Needed)
.TP
.B 70.0% \- 79.9%
Grade C (Fair Posture / Several Deficiencies)
.TP
.B 60.0% \- 69.9%
Grade D (Poor Posture / Significant Risk)
.TP
.B Below 60.0%
Grade F (Critical Risk / Urgent Remediation Required)
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Successful scan execution. All checks passed, or the Hardening Index meets the
acceptable threshold without unhandled errors.
.TP
.B 1
Audit completed with critical security failures, hardening score below
acceptable threshold, invalid command-line invocation, or running on an
unsupported operating system.
.TP
.B 2
Insufficient permissions to execute certain checks or remediations, or
operation interrupted by user (SIGINT/SIGTERM).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to any non-empty value, disables colorized ANSI terminal output
(equivalent to \fB\-\-no\-color\fR).
.TP
.B MACHAR_NO_COLOR
When set to 1, forces monochrome terminal mode.
.TP
.B MACHAR_QUIET
When set to 1, suppresses detailed check output and displays only summary
results.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/macharden
The primary executable wrapper and orchestrator.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/macharden/
Directory containing core engine modules and category check scripts:
.RS
.TP
.I ui.sh
Terminal styling, ANSI palettes, progress displays, and banners.
.TP
.I engine.sh
Check registry, execution loop, scoring calculations, and state tracking.
.TP
.I report.sh
Terminal, JSON, Markdown, and HTML report formatters.
.TP
.I remediate.sh
Interactive remediation runner and fix script generator.
.TP
.I audit_*.sh
Modular security check definitions for hardening, network, secrets, and
persistence.
.RE
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/macharden.1
UNIX manual page.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/zsh/site-functions/_macharden
Native Zsh autocompletion definition.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/bash-completion/completions/macharden
Native Bash autocompletion script.
.SH EXAMPLES
Execute a full security audit with default colorized terminal output:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden
.RE
.PP
Audit only the system hardening domain:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden \-c hardening
.RE
.PP
Audit network exposure and export findings to a Markdown report:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden \-c network \-f markdown \-o network_audit.md
.RE
.PP
Run full audit, output structured JSON for SIEM or automated pipelines, and
suppress terminal banners:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden \-f json \-o audit_results.json \-q
.RE
.PP
Generate a responsive HTML report for executive presentation:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden \-f html \-o security_report.html
.RE
.PP
Audit host compliance against the CIS Apple macOS Benchmark:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden \-\-compliance cis
.RE
.PP
Inspect security posture and generate a standalone remediation shell script
without modifying system state:
.RS
.PP
.B macharden \-\-generate\-fix fix_hardening.sh
.RE
.PP
Interactively review and apply remediation fixes for detected vulnerabilities:
.RS
.PP
.B sudo macharden \-\-fix
.RE
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B macharden
is strictly non-destructive during standard audit execution. Reading
configuration state via \fBdefaults\fR, \fBspctl\fR, \fBcsrutil\fR,
\fBlaunchctl\fR, and network socket inspection does not alter any system files
or runtime states.
.PP
Remediations applied via \fB\-\-fix\fR or through scripts created by
\fB\-\-generate\-fix\fR frequently modify system preferences, firewall settings,
or launch daemons. Administrative privileges (\fBsudo\fR) are required for
applying remediations. Always review generated remediation scripts before
executing them in production environments.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Tested and verified on:
.IP \(bu 3
macOS 15 Sequoia
.IP \(bu 3
macOS 14 Sonoma
.IP \(bu 3
macOS 13 Ventura
.IP \(bu 3
macOS 12 Monterey
.PP
Architectures: Apple Silicon (ARM64: M1/M2/M3/M4) and Intel (x86_64).
